==Catseye Additional Level Limit==
:''For more information, see the [[Catseye]] page.''

To increase a Cat Unit's level limit with Catseyes, the Cat Unit must have reached level 30 first (except for Normal Cats, which they cannot be used on). The additional level limit also needs XP to level up and every Catseye will increase the level limit by one level. The upper limit is level 50 for non-Uber Rares, but with Dark Catseyes, Uber Rares can reach '''level 60'''.

==Best Ways to Get Higher Ranks==
*The purchasable Special Cats are quite cheap to upgrade. Consider buying a few of them, especially when they are at half price. Their XP costs after level 30 still retain the same affordability, so using Special Catseyes (which are in abundance by mid-game) to gain extra user rank isn't a bad idea.
*Certain [[Million Downloads Event]]s will run "Half XP Cost" events on Friday, Saturday and Sunday (or more rarely for several full weeks), which makes upgrading Cats only cost half as much XP.
*Prioritize cheaper upgrades, but remember that every 10 levels, the upgrading cost is massively reduced (except for [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed Cats]] and [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]]).
*Besides [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP Stages]], [[Legend Stages]] are very efficient for farming XP.
*The "Sort By Level" feature lets you sort from lowest level to highest level, which can help with finding cheap upgrades.
*Grinding +levels for [[:Category:Event Capsule Cats|Event Capsule Cats]] or [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] can also help to massively increase User Rank. For example, [[Heartbeat Catcademy (Event Gacha)|Heartbeat Catcademy]] will increase User Rank by 194 if all the Event Capsule Cats are gotten to their maximum level.

==Exceptions and Notes==
*[[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline]]'s + level increase comes at a separate User Rank than the other Normal Cats. Superfeline's + level cannot be increased above +9 until User Rank 10001 is reached, by which point the rest of the Normal Cats can already go to +90.
*The Cat Cannon Range can only be leveled up to 10 and there are no Capsule upgrades for it.
*The level caps for [[:Category:Event Capsule Cats|Event Capsule Cats]] tend to vary. Li'l Cats can be upgraded to level MAX+60, [[Heartbeat Catcademy (Event Gacha)|Heartbeat Academy]] units max out at 1+50 except for [[Class Rep Cat (Special Cat)|Class Rep Cat]] who maxes out at 1+40, [[Summer Break Cats (Event Gacha)|Summer Break Cats]] units max out at MAX+40 except [[Ancient Egg: N202 (Special Cat)|Armored Firefly Cat]] and [[Farmer Cat (Special Cat)|Farmer Cat]], who max out at MAX+20, etc.
*There have been reports of bugs with the User Rank system. Examples found in Reddit discussions include players being able to increase units beyond specified + levels without having reached the necessary rank or the notice presented when clicking the Mission icon will indicate there is no further rank to currently achieve. This may have occurred if you played the game on Version 2, and upon getting Version 3, you auto-obtained all the new rewards. It should have been fixed around [[Version 5.0 Update|Version 5.0]].
*Sometimes, you may have the Cat Combos unlocked at Rank 2700 upon unlocking Cat Combos.
*Some Cats can be upgraded beyond the player's current level cap, such as the [[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event|Madoka Magica]] Uber Rares which can reach level 10+19 before clearing Chapter 2.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] cannot be upgraded past level 20, regardless of how high the player's user rank is.
*[[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]]'s XP cost scaling is similar to Cat, rather than standard [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cats]].

